france is experiencing its worst ever  recorded drought more than two-thirds of  departments in the country are now at  crisis level  and last week the government said around  a hundred towns had completely run out  of water and that means trucks like this  one are coming up and delivering water  so the water is coming through this pipe  going into the building here which  surrounds a borehole which is now  completely dry so eight times a day they  deliver the water which is then pumped  down to the town below  [Music]  you can see here how dry the ground is  so why is the drought so bad well one of  the problems here is that the winter was  drier so there wasn't as much snow on  the mountains there wasn't as much rain  and then the water sources have been  decimated by the long  hot summer so far there are warnings  that some areas could be experiencing  drought until the end of the year  so this is a big problem for lots of  people across france there are water  restrictions in place so in this town  for example you can see the fountain is  off people are limited to using 200  liters per day and they're not allowed  to water their gardens or fill up their  pools for example and they're also  massive issues for farmers some of whom  are seeing a drop in the yields of their  crops  so how do you solve a problem as big as  this well as well as bringing water to  those in need another thing that's being  focused on is re-educating people to get  them to cut down on wasting water so  collecting rain for example but experts  tell us as climate change continues  we're likely to have more extreme  droughts like this
 

